  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since ${v}_{1}={v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}-{v}_{4},$ we have that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot {v}_{1}+(-1)\\cdot {v}_{2}+(-5)\\cdot {v}_{3}+1\\cdot {v}_{4}=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution and the set ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent by definition.\n\n- Statement II is false.  Since ${v}_{1}={v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}-{v}_{4},$ the equation ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${v}_{1}={v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}-{v}_{4},$ we have that\n\n$$\n{v}_{4}={v}_{2}+5{v}_{3}-{v}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThat is, ${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
